From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DolphinSlicer <build@localhost>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 04:16:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/9] Platform: recognise Emscripten/WebAssembly

detect_platform() hit the 'Unknown platform detected' static_assert when compiled with
Emscripten. Report Platform::Unknown / PlatformFlavor::Unknown there; libslic3r only
consults the platform flavor for a ChromeOS (LinuxOnChromium) special case.
Upstreamable: yes.
---
 src/libslic3r/Platform.cpp | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/libslic3r/Platform.cpp b/src/libslic3r/Platform.cpp
index 35a30712..7bc75d53 100644
--- a/src/libslic3r/Platform.cpp
+++ b/src/libslic3r/Platform.cpp
@@ -91,6 +91,11 @@ void detect_platform()
     BOOST_LOG_TRIVIAL(info) << "Platform: OpenBSD";
 	s_platform 		  = Platform::BSDUnix;
 	s_platform_flavor = PlatformFlavor::OpenBSD;
+#elif defined(__EMSCRIPTEN__)
+	// WebAssembly (browser or Node): no host OS to detect.
+    BOOST_LOG_TRIVIAL(info) << "Platform: WebAssembly";
+	s_platform 		  = Platform::Unknown;
+	s_platform_flavor = PlatformFlavor::Unknown;
 #else
 	// This should not happen.
     BOOST_LOG_TRIVIAL(info) << "Platform: Unknown";
